  ─ Cost is what this usage would cost at API rates, not what you were billed;
    Claude Code on a subscription draws from your plan allowance instead.
  ─ Water assumes 0.30 mL / 1k tokens, a rough estimate. See README.
  ─ 1 model had no rate and was excluded from the cost total: claude-imaginary-9.
    Add it to pricing.json to price it.
  ─ 3 records carried no cache-write TTL split; those writes were billed as
    5-minute writes, which understates any that were really 1-hour writes.
  ─ 1 request used fast mode, which bills at roughly double the standard rate.
  ─ 1 request pinned inference to the US, which adds 10% to every token class.
  ─ 1 request ran on the batch tier at half the standard rate.
  ─ Includes 12 web searches. Failed searches are not billed but are
    indistinguishable here, so that charge is an upper bound.
  ─ 1 record had no usable timestamp and is counted in the totals but not by day.
